{{Term/Store|Temperature|Temperatures|Series, BotW, TotK}} is a recurring gameplay mechanic in {{TLoZ Series}}.<ref>{{Cite|{{Big|Temperature Changes}}<br/>The temperature will change depending on your location and the time of day. It's a good idea to pay close attention to fluctuations in temperature when you're out roaming.|Tips and Tricks|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|{{Big|Temperature Changes}}<br/>The temperature will change depending on your location and the time of day. It's a good idea to pay close attention to fluctuations in temperature when you're out roaming.|Tips and Tricks|TotK}}</ref>{{Name Ref|OoT3D, SSHD, EoW}}

==Overview==
==={{OoT|-}}===
Temperature is briefly used within the [[Death Mountain Crater]] and sections of the [[Fire Temple]] to hinder [[Link]]'s progression. When exposed to the [[Scorching Climate]], a timer will appear and will cause Link to die unless he is revived by a [[Fairy]]. However, this can be prevented by wearing the [[Goron Tunic]], allowing Link to stay cool indefinitely and survive the scorching heat. The amount of time Link has is eight seconds for every [[Heart]] in his [[Life Gauge]] when the timer appears.

==={{SS|-}}===
Link is incapable of entering places with high Temperatures like the [[Volcano Summit]], but this time [[Link]] is slowly damaged catches fire instead being subjected to a timer. To stay cool when entering areas with high Temperatures, Link must obtain the [[Fireshield Earrings]] from [[Din's Silent Realm]] trial.

==={{BotW|-}}===
{{Main|Heat, Freezing Climate, Scorching Climate}}
Unlike in the previous games, Temperature is now a gameplay mechanic featured everywhere around [[Hyrule Kingdom]], and Link can check the Temperature with a dial on the bottom-right screen or opening his [[Sheikah Slate]] and viewing the [[Map]] section with actual measurements. When exposed to extreme Temperatures, Link will begin to take damage, but can prevent this by going to a more temperate area, entering bodies of [[Water]] in [[Scorching Climate]]s, equipping an elemental [[Weapon]], wearing certain [[Armor]], or eating [[Food]] with status effects.

When the Temperature drops below {{Exp|0°C|32°F}}, Link will experience a basic level of cold Temperature that will slowly damage him. When the Temperature drops below {{Exp|-10°C|14°F}}, Link will experience an advanced level of cold Temperature and will take damage more quickly. Certain bodies of water in [[Freezing Climate]]s will cause Link to quickly take damage; no armor, elixir nor food can offer protection against this. Similarly, when the Temperature rises above {{Exp|40°C|104°F}}, Link will experience a basic level of [[Heat]], he will also slowly sustain damage. When the Temperature rises above {{Exp|50°C|122°F}}, Link will experience an advanced level of Heat and take damage more quickly. Places that contain lava flows raise Temperatures significantly beyond normal Heat, the Sheikah Slate will malfunction and read "ERROR". Additionally, Link and any wooden equipment exposed to the environment will begin to catch fire.

==={{TotK|-}}===
Temperature is present all throughout [[Hyrule]] and the [[Sky Island]]s above it. Some locations are too cold for [[Link]] to withstand without special [[Armor]] or other protective measures.

